== CANON-12 (r3.76): `IIf(C, A, B)` selects a value (formerly `if C then A
== else B`, ADR-0013). Each branch is an expression; only the chosen branch is
== evaluated; it nests, and it may span lines.
Clamp(X Integer, Limit Integer) Integer :
    Return IIf(X < 0, -X, IIf(X > Limit, Limit, X))
;

Main :
    Limit := 10
    Result := IIf(Limit < 0,
                  -Limit,
                  IIf(Limit > 5, 5, Limit))
    Level := IIf(Result >= 5, "high", "low")
    PutLn(Result, " ", Level, " ", Clamp(-3, 10), " ", Clamp(42, 10))
;
